1
00:00:01,559 --> 00:00:03,360
[♪♪]

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:05,080
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,960
This is my little brother,
George.

4
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,160
[GRUNTS]

5
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,400
This is Mommy Pig.

6
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,559
[SNORTS]

7
00:00:10,559 --> 00:00:11,719
And this is Daddy Pig.

8
00:00:11,719 --> 00:00:13,360
[GRUNTS]
[ALL LAUGHING]

9
00:00:14,319 --> 00:00:15,840
Peppa Pig.

10
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:19,400
[♪♪]

11
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,759
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

12
00:00:21,759 --> 00:00:24,959
NARRATOR:
Granny Pig and Grandpa Pig
are making lunch,

13
00:00:24,959 --> 00:00:26,279
for Peppa and her family.

14
00:00:26,279 --> 00:00:29,880
[SNORTS]
I've dug up some more potatoes.

15
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,799
Oh, Grandpa.

16
00:00:31,799 --> 00:00:34,280
We've already got
plenty of potatoes.

17
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,199
You can never have
too many potatoes.

18
00:00:37,199 --> 00:00:40,000
Okay. But get the potatoes
in the oven.

19
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,839
The others
will be here soon.

20
00:00:41,839 --> 00:00:44,680
[LAUGHS]
We've plenty of time.

21
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,680
It's only 11:00.

22
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,360
[♪♪]

23
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:51,320
Peppa and her family
are on their way.

24
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:53,040
I wish we'd set off sooner.

25
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:54,800
We're going
to be late again.

26
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,919
Don't worry, Mommy Pig.
We've still got loads of time.

27
00:00:58,919 --> 00:01:00,839
We're always late

28
00:01:00,839 --> 00:01:03,919
when we go to
Granny and Grandpa's.

29
00:01:03,919 --> 00:01:05,679
[CHUCKLES]
Not this time.

30
00:01:05,679 --> 00:01:09,160
I've found a new way
that avoids all the traffic.

31
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:10,479
[TIRES SCREECH]

32
00:01:10,479 --> 00:01:13,960
Oh. I wasn't
expecting that.

33
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:17,720
Peppa and her family
are stuck in a traffic jam.

34
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:22,399
Look, there's Danny Dog
and Granddad Dog.

35
00:01:22,399 --> 00:01:25,440
Danny Dog and Granddad Dog
are in the traffic jam too.

36
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,160
Hello, Peppa.
Hello, Peppa!

37
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,640
[BARKS]

38
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:32,560
We're going to my Granny
and Grandpa's for lunch.

39
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,600
We're going to be late.

40
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:37,520
[CLOCK CHIMES]

41
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,360
It's 1:00.

42
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:42,399
They're late.
As usual.

43
00:01:42,399 --> 00:01:44,880
[SNORTS]
How are your potatoes doing?

44
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:48,720
Um, they still need
a bit more cooking.

45
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:51,479
[RINGS]

46
00:01:51,479 --> 00:01:53,080
Granny Pig speaking.

47
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,320
Hello, Granny Pig.

48
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,880
[SNORTS]
We're stuck in a traffic jam.

49
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,280
Don't worry.
We're running late too.

50
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:02,839
Grandpa's gone over the top
with potatoes. See you in a bit.

51
00:02:02,839 --> 00:02:06,199
The poor dears are stuck
in a traffic jam.

52
00:02:06,199 --> 00:02:10,359
Sounds like I've got time
to get a few more potatoes.

53
00:02:10,359 --> 00:02:11,560
Grandpa Pig.

54
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:15,280
PEPPA:
We're moving so slowly.

55
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:18,959
We'll never get
to Granny and Grandpa's.

56
00:02:18,959 --> 00:02:21,359
Peppa's right. We have
to try a different way.

57
00:02:21,359 --> 00:02:23,680
But there aren't
any other main roads.

58
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,239
I know a shortcut.

59
00:02:25,239 --> 00:02:27,200
[TIRES SCREECH]

60
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,799
Bye-bye, everyone.
We're taking a shortcut.

61
00:02:30,799 --> 00:02:33,000
Bye-bye, Peppa!
Good luck!

62
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,799
Mommy Pig is taking a shortcut
to get ahead of the traffic.

63
00:02:36,799 --> 00:02:39,079
The shortcut
is very bumpy.

64
00:02:39,079 --> 00:02:42,799
[GIGGLES]
This is fun.

65
00:02:42,799 --> 00:02:44,720
Are you sure about this?

66
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,920
Trust me.
Hello, ducks!

67
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,760
We're taking a shortcut.
[SNORTS]

68
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,200
[ALL QUACK]

69
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:55,840
Look, there's
the main road again.

70
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,120
Well done, Mommy Pig.

71
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:02,040
But we're still behind
Danny's lorry.

72
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:04,519
Hello.
Welcome back.

73
00:03:04,519 --> 00:03:09,359
Oh, dear. Mommy Pig's shortcut
has not worked very well.

74
00:03:09,359 --> 00:03:11,959
[CHIMES]

75
00:03:11,959 --> 00:03:13,679
Good. Lunch is ready.

76
00:03:13,679 --> 00:03:18,280
And, most important of all,
the potatoes are done.

77
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,760
Lunch is ready,

78
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,679
but Peppa and her family
are still not here.

79
00:03:22,679 --> 00:03:24,079
[PHONE RINGS]

80
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,120
Grandpa Pig speaking.

81
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,600
We're almost at your house.

82
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:34,079
But the traffic is still moving
at the speed of a snail.

83
00:03:34,079 --> 00:03:38,640
A very,
very slow snail.

84
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,600
They're almost here.

85
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:43,160
But they're still
in the traffic jam.

86
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:44,359
Poor dears.

87
00:03:44,359 --> 00:03:46,880
The food is going
to get cold.

88
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:51,560
I've got an idea.
I'll get my wheelbarrow.

89
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,359
What is Grandpa Pig doing?

90
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:56,280
Granny Pig.
[SNORTS]

91
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:59,920
Load the lunch
into the wheelbarrow.

92
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:01,839
Aye, aye, Grandpa Pig.

93
00:04:03,399 --> 00:04:05,799
If they can't come
to the lunch,

94
00:04:05,799 --> 00:04:08,119
we have to take
the lunch to them.

95
00:04:08,119 --> 00:04:09,880
[LAUGHS]

96
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,679
Look.

97
00:04:11,679 --> 00:04:17,479
There's Granny and Grandpa with
our lunch in a wheelbarrow.

98
00:04:17,479 --> 00:04:19,000
Ahoy, there.

99
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,440
[SNORTS]
Lunch is served.

100
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:24,280
Is there enough
for Danny

101
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:26,920
and Granddad Dog
to have some too?

102
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:29,200
We've got enough
for everyone.

103
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:31,440
ALL:
Hooray! Potatoes!

104
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:32,960
[ALL LAUGH]

105
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:36,240
Good job you did lots and lots
of potatoes, Grandpa.

106
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,479
[LAUGHS]

107
00:04:37,479 --> 00:04:41,240
You can never have
too many potatoes.

108
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,719
[ALL LAUGHING]

109
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,760
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

110
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:52,520
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

111
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:56,719
NARRATOR:
It is almost bedtime.

112
00:04:56,719 --> 00:04:59,400
Peppa and George are just
finishing their supper.

113
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,560
[YAWNS]
Daddy Pig.

114
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,320
[BOTH GIGGLING]
Oh, sorry.

115
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:06,240
I'm a bit tired.
It's been a long day.

116
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,880
George and I are aren't
sleepy at all.

117
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,599
Can we play
in the garden?

118
00:05:10,599 --> 00:05:12,599
But it's almost
your bedtime.

119
00:05:12,599 --> 00:05:15,800
Can we play outside
for just a tiny bit?

120
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,320
Please, Mommy.
Please, Daddy.

121
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,440
[LAUGHS]
All right.

122
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:23,159
But you must come in when
we call you for your bath.

123
00:05:23,159 --> 00:05:24,960
[BOTH GIGGLING]

124
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,599
I don't know where they get
their energy from.

125
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:31,479
Peppa and George are playing
one last game outside

126
00:05:31,479 --> 00:05:32,800
before bedtime.

127
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,479
Look, George.

128
00:05:34,479 --> 00:05:36,280
Lots of muddy puddles.

129
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:37,680
[SNORTS]

130
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:39,919
Peppa and George are wearing
their boots.

131
00:05:39,919 --> 00:05:42,719
They are going to jump up
and down in muddy puddles.

132
00:05:42,719 --> 00:05:44,320
[GIGGLES]

133
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:46,919
Peppa loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

134
00:05:46,919 --> 00:05:48,680
[LAUGHS]

135
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:51,479
George loves jumping
up and down in muddy puddles.

136
00:05:51,479 --> 00:05:53,039
[LAUGHING]

137
00:05:53,039 --> 00:05:54,240
[SNORTS]

138
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,400
Look!

139
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:58,479
The biggest puddle
in the world!

140
00:05:58,479 --> 00:06:00,479
What a huge, big puddle.

141
00:06:00,479 --> 00:06:02,280
[BOTH LAUGHING]

142
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:09,359
Peppa, George, bath time!

143
00:06:09,359 --> 00:06:10,800
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

144
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,159
Daddy, Mommy,

145
00:06:12,159 --> 00:06:15,280
we found the biggest muddy
puddle in the world.

146
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:16,719
I can see that.

147
00:06:16,719 --> 00:06:18,280
Quick, into the bath.

148
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:21,400
Oh. Can't we just play
outside a bit longer?

149
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:22,599
[DADDY PIG LAUGHS]

150
00:06:22,599 --> 00:06:25,120
No. It's bath time.

151
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,440
[BOTH GIGGLE]

152
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:31,760
Are you and George
feeling sleepy?

153
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:32,960
No, Daddy.

154
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:35,919
We are not even
a tiny bit sleepy.

155
00:06:35,919 --> 00:06:38,960
[BOTH GIGGLING]

156
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:42,359
Peppa and George might
not be sleepy, but I am.

157
00:06:42,359 --> 00:06:44,799
Me too.
[YAWNS]

158
00:06:44,799 --> 00:06:48,320
Before bedtime, Peppa
and George have their bath.

159
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:50,440
[SPLASHING, GIGGLING]

160
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,960
Peppa likes splashing.

161
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:54,159
George likes splashing.

162
00:06:54,159 --> 00:06:57,640
Peppa and George
both like splashing.

163
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:58,840
[LAUGHS]

164
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,719
That's enough splashing.

165
00:07:00,719 --> 00:07:02,799
Let's get you dry
and into pajamas.

166
00:07:02,799 --> 00:07:05,120
Oh, can't we just
stay in the bath

167
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:08,039
a little bit longer?
[SNORTS]

168
00:07:08,039 --> 00:07:09,640
Bath time is over.

169
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:12,239
Now it's time
to clean your teeth.

170
00:07:12,239 --> 00:07:14,320
Before going to bed,

171
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:16,280
Peppa and George
brush their teeth.

172
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:18,280
[GIGGLES]
[BUBBLES FIZZ]

173
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,440
[LAUGHING]
[BUBBLES FIZZING]

174
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,359
Okay, that's enough
brushing.

175
00:07:22,359 --> 00:07:23,799
[SNORTS]
Into your beds.

176
00:07:23,799 --> 00:07:27,520
Oh. I think our teeth
need a bit more cleaning.

177
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:30,960
When you're in bed,
Daddy Pig will read you a story.

178
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,640
Hooray!
[SNORTS]

179
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:34,880
Peppa and George
like stories.

180
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:36,919
[SNORTING]

181
00:07:36,919 --> 00:07:39,120
When Peppa goes to bed,

182
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,960
she always has her Teddy
tucked up with her.

183
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:44,039
When George goes to bed,
he always has

184
00:07:44,039 --> 00:07:46,280
Mr. Dinosaur
tucked up with him.

185
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:49,000
[SNORTS]
Are you feeling sleepy now?

186
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,159
No, Daddy.

187
00:07:50,159 --> 00:07:53,000
We need lots and lots
of stories.

188
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,440
Daddy Pig will read you
one story.

189
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,880
Now which book
do you want?

190
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,560
Um...
[SNORTS]

191
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:00,960
"The Red Monkey" book.
[DADDY PIG LAUGHS]

192
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:04,679
Okay, I'll read you
"The Red Monkey" book.

193
00:08:04,679 --> 00:08:07,760
Peppa and George like
"The Red Monkey" book.

194
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,440
"Once upon a time...

195
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:11,799
[YAWNS]
Oh, sorry, Daddy Pig.

196
00:08:11,799 --> 00:08:13,479
[BOTH SNICKER]

197
00:08:14,679 --> 00:08:17,400
"Once upon a time,
there was a red monkey.

198
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:22,400
"And this red monkey
had a bath.

199
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:25,440
"And cleaned his teeth.

200
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:27,120
"He got into his bed.

201
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:29,960
"And soon he fell fast asleep.

202
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:32,959
"Good night, red monkey.

203
00:08:32,959 --> 00:08:35,520
[BOTH SNORING]
Peppa and George are asleep.

204
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:38,880
Good night, Peppa and George.
Sleep well.

205
00:08:40,079 --> 00:08:42,799
[BOTH YAWN]

206
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:44,959
Now Peppa and George
are asleep,

207
00:08:44,959 --> 00:08:49,280
Mommy Pig and Daddy Pig are
going to watch some television.

208
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:53,160
TV ANNOUNCER:
And now it's time for
The Amazing Mr. Potato.

209
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:56,120
I've been looking forward
to watching this program.

210
00:08:56,120 --> 00:09:00,040
The Amazing Mr. Potato
is always ready for action.

211
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:04,360
He runs fast,
he jumps high, he never sleeps.

212
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:07,680
[BOTH YAWN AND SNORE]

213
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:09,840
It is bedtime
for Peppa and George.

214
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:13,680
And it looks like it is bedtime
for Mommy and Daddy too.

215
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:15,319
[MOMMY &amp; DADDY PIG SNORE]

216
00:09:17,839 --> 00:09:20,360
[♪♪]

217
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,800
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

218
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,319
NARRATOR:
Today is the school
sports day.

219
00:09:25,319 --> 00:09:26,640
[KIDS LAUGHING]

220
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:28,640
Peppa and her friends
are all here.

221
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:30,360
The first event is running.

222
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:31,839
[ALL GIGGLE]

223
00:09:31,839 --> 00:09:34,240
The children have to run
as fast as they can.

224
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:37,360
I think I will win.
I can run very fast.

225
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:40,600
[BLEATS]
I'm faster than you.

226
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:44,480
Ready, steady, go.

227
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:47,400
I can run at
a hundred miles an hour.

228
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:49,959
I can run at
a million miles an hour.

229
00:09:49,959 --> 00:09:53,439
Peppa! Suzy!
Stop talking and run!

230
00:09:53,439 --> 00:09:55,120
Oh.

231
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:57,520
Rebecca Rabbit
is in the lead.

232
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,079
[BOTH PANTING]
Oh, dear.

233
00:09:59,079 --> 00:10:01,319
Peppa and Suzy
are right at the back.

234
00:10:01,319 --> 00:10:04,199
[ALL SHOUTING]

235
00:10:04,199 --> 00:10:06,800
[SQUEAK]
Rebecca Rabbit wins.

236
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:08,360
[ALL GIGGLING]

237
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:11,360
And Peppa and Suzy
are last.

238
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,880
[BOTH PANTING]

239
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:17,280
The winner of the race
is Rebecca Rabbit.

240
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,280
ALL:
Hooray!

241
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:20,680
Squeak! Thank you.

242
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,040
[GIGGLES]

243
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:23,800
[BOTH PANTING]

244
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:28,319
I would have won if you hadn't
been talking to me, Suzy.

245
00:10:28,319 --> 00:10:30,120
Now, now, Peppa.

246
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:33,839
Remember, it's not winning
that matters, but taking part.

247
00:10:33,839 --> 00:10:35,400
Yes, Daddy.

248
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:38,360
The next event
is the long jump.

249
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,040
[BOTH LAUGH]

250
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:43,360
George and Richard have to see
who can jump the furthest.

251
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:48,800
George, run as fast as you can,
then jump as far as you can.

252
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,079
[SNORTS]

253
00:10:50,079 --> 00:10:54,040
MADAME GAZELLE:
George, ready, steady, go.

254
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:56,480
[GIGGLING]

255
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:58,760
George has jumped
as far as he can.

256
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,640
And now,
it's Richard Rabbit's turn.

257
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:04,000
[SQUEAKS]

258
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:08,400
If Richard doesn't run,
he won't jump very far.

259
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,280
MADAME GAZELLE:
Richard Rabbit,

260
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:11,760
ready, steady, go.

261
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:15,800
Richard Rabbit has jumped
further than George.

262
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:19,160
And the winner,
is Richard Rabbit.

263
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,719
CROWD:
Hooray!

264
00:11:20,719 --> 00:11:23,240
[CHUCKLES]
[CRIES]

265
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:25,839
George, remember,

266
00:11:25,839 --> 00:11:27,800
it's not the winning
that matters,

267
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:31,240
but taking part.
[WHIMPERS]

268
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:33,800
The next race is the relay.

269
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:38,079
Each child needs to pick
a parent to race with.

270
00:11:38,079 --> 00:11:40,319
Peppa, pick me, pick me.

271
00:11:40,319 --> 00:11:43,480
But Daddy, you're not
very good at running.

272
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:46,079
I was very good when
I was a little piggy.

273
00:11:46,079 --> 00:11:48,160
But now you have
a big tummy.

274
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:51,880
But I can still
touch my toes...nearly.

275
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:55,199
[CHUCKLES]
All right, Daddy.

276
00:11:55,199 --> 00:11:59,079
But you must run very fast.
[CHUCKLES]

277
00:11:59,079 --> 00:12:02,600
The Mommies and Daddies will
run the first part of the race,

278
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:05,280
and then hand the batons
to the children.

279
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:10,719
Mommies and Daddies.
Ready, steady, go.

280
00:12:10,719 --> 00:12:13,000
[ALL SHOUTING]

281
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,719
Daddy Pig is in the lead.

282
00:12:15,719 --> 00:12:18,480
[ALL CHEERING]
PEPPA: Come on, Daddy!

283
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:21,360
Thank you, Daddy.
You did very well.

284
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:25,120
Now it's my turn to take--
Peppa, stop talking and run!

285
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,439
Oh!

286
00:12:27,439 --> 00:12:29,600
[ALL MAKING ANIMAL NOISES]

287
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,360
[PANTING]

288
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:33,959
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

289
00:12:33,959 --> 00:12:36,120
[TRUMPETING]

290
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:38,880
And the winner
is Emily Elephant.

291
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:40,760
ALL:
Hooray!

292
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,400
[PANTING]
Oh, Daddy.

293
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:46,520
[SNORTS]
I haven't won a prize yet.

294
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:49,959
Don't worry, Peppa.
There's still one more event.

295
00:12:49,959 --> 00:12:53,439
And now for the last event
of the day:

296
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,240
the tug-of-war.

297
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,959
Boys against girls.

298
00:12:56,959 --> 00:12:59,000
[ALL LAUGH]

299
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:04,240
When I say go, you must pull
the rope with all your strength.

300
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:06,480
[SNORTS]
The girls will win.

301
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:07,839
[BARKS]
No they won't.

302
00:13:07,839 --> 00:13:09,719
The boys will win.

303
00:13:09,719 --> 00:13:13,000
MADAME GAZELLE:
Ready, steady, go.

304
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,480
[ALL STRAINING]

305
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,319
ALL:
Come on, boys!

306
00:13:16,319 --> 00:13:18,160
Come on, pull!

307
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,680
ALL:
Come on, girls!

308
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:22,480
Pull!
I am pulling!

309
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:26,719
Everyone is pulling so hard,
the rope is breaking.

310
00:13:26,719 --> 00:13:28,040
ALL:
Whoa!

311
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:30,680
[ALL LAUGH]

312
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:35,360
And the result is a draw,
so both teams win.

313
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,240
ALL:
Hooray!

314
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:39,920
[SNORTS]
I love the school sports day.

315
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:42,280
Especially when
I win a prize.

316
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,599
[CHUCKLES]

317
00:13:43,599 --> 00:13:45,839
[ALL LAUGH]

318
00:13:48,839 --> 00:13:52,400
[♪♪]

319
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:54,319
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

320
00:13:54,319 --> 00:13:58,640
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George are playing
with Pedro Pony.

321
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:00,880
They are going to jump
in muddy puddles.

322
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:03,760
[ALL LAUGHING]

323
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:07,480
Oh! Ooh!

324
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:11,120
Pedro has slipped
and lost his glasses.

325
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:13,240
[NEIGHS]
Where are my glasses?

326
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,800
Without glasses,
Pedro cannot see very well.

327
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,560
Whoa...

328
00:14:18,599 --> 00:14:19,880
[SNORTS]

329
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:22,199
George has found
Pedro's glasses.

330
00:14:22,199 --> 00:14:23,439
Ooh.

331
00:14:23,439 --> 00:14:24,839
[SNICKERS]

332
00:14:24,839 --> 00:14:27,160
[SNORTS]
Silly George.

333
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:29,640
Here they are.
Thank you.

334
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:33,160
[SNORTS]
Pedro, why do you
wear glasses?

335
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:36,560
I need to.
The optician says so.

336
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:38,599
What's an optician?

337
00:14:38,599 --> 00:14:40,839
My Daddy
is an optician.

338
00:14:40,839 --> 00:14:43,040
He checks that you
can see clearly.

339
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:45,760
How? Does he look
inside your head?

340
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,040
[LAUGHS]

341
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,760
He does an eye test.

342
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:50,680
Shall I give you
an eye test?

343
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,959
Yes. Give me
an eye test.

344
00:14:52,959 --> 00:14:55,479
Okay.

345
00:14:55,479 --> 00:14:58,079
Hmm. Interesting.

346
00:14:58,079 --> 00:15:01,439
Close one eye
and say what you see.

347
00:15:01,439 --> 00:15:04,040
I can see...George.

348
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,760
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

349
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:08,479
Now close both eyes.

350
00:15:08,479 --> 00:15:10,880
Now I can't see
anything.

351
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:15,520
Hmm, can't see anything.
Very, very interesting.

352
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:17,599
I think you
need glasses.

353
00:15:17,599 --> 00:15:20,680
Oh, do I?
Yes.

354
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:22,760
Pedro! Home time!

355
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,319
[KIDS GIGGLE]

356
00:15:24,319 --> 00:15:25,800
Bye-bye, Pedro.

357
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,920
[NEIGHS]
Bye-bye.

358
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,160
[ENGINE STARTS]

359
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:32,800
[SNORTS]
Mommy, I need glasses.

360
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,160
What?

361
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:37,680
Pedro gave me an eye test
and I need glasses.

362
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,839
I'm sure your eyes
are fine.

363
00:15:39,839 --> 00:15:44,760
No, Mommy, when I closed my
eyes, I couldn't see anything.

364
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:48,079
But no one can see anything
with their eyes closed.

365
00:15:48,079 --> 00:15:49,360
Oh.

366
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,640
What's this about
needing glasses?

367
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:54,040
Pedro knows
all about glasses.

368
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:56,479
His Daddy
is an optician.

369
00:15:56,479 --> 00:15:59,280
All right, Peppa.
Let's take you to the optician

370
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:01,000
for a proper eye test.

371
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,079
[LAUGHS]
Let's go now.

372
00:16:03,079 --> 00:16:04,520
[GIGGLES AND SNORTS]

373
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:07,240
George, would you like
an eye test too?

374
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,479
No.

375
00:16:08,479 --> 00:16:10,199
[ALL LAUGH]

376
00:16:10,199 --> 00:16:13,479
[♪♪]

377
00:16:13,479 --> 00:16:15,160
Peppa is at the optician's.

378
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,520
[NEIGHS]

379
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:18,240
Mr. Pony is the optician.

380
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:21,040
Hello, Peppa.
Please sit down.

381
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,400
[LAUGHS]

382
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,400
Now, what can I do
for you?

383
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:27,520
[SNORTS]
I need an eye test, please.

384
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:29,199
Of course.

385
00:16:29,199 --> 00:16:30,959
Put these
special glasses on,

386
00:16:30,959 --> 00:16:32,760
and then look at the chart.

387
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:35,479
Mr. Pony is going
to test Peppa's eyes.

388
00:16:35,479 --> 00:16:37,800
Can you read these letters
for me, please?

389
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:40,199
Okay. Um...

390
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:43,319
A, B, C,

391
00:16:43,319 --> 00:16:46,400
D, E, F.

392
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:49,400
Good. Now these
numbers, please.

393
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,680
Um...

394
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:53,280
1, 2, 3,

395
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:56,240
4, 5, 6.

396
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:57,520
MR. PONY:
Very good.

397
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,680
[GIGGLES]

398
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:01,240
And now these colors,
please.

399
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:05,000
PEPPA:
Red, green, orange, blue,

400
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,960
yellow, purple.

401
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:09,319
Excellent. While I check
your results,

402
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:11,480
would you like
to choose some glasses?

403
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,599
Yes, please.

404
00:17:12,599 --> 00:17:15,800
How about these
glasses, Peppa?

405
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:20,680
They're funny.
[BOTH LAUGH]

406
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,480
I know, what about
these ones?

407
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:26,040
They're too big.

408
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:28,200
[BOTH LAUGH]

409
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,919
How about these?

410
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:35,360
Wow. I like these ones,
Mommy.

411
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:38,320
MOMMY PIG:
Yes, Peppa, you look fantastic.

412
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,399
[SNORTS]
I look fantastic.

413
00:17:41,399 --> 00:17:43,080
[BOTH LAUGH]

414
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:44,320
[CLEARS THROAT]

415
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:45,600
Good news.

416
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,680
Peppa has perfect eyesight.

417
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:50,240
Oh, so I don't
need glasses?

418
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,520
MR. PONY:
No.

419
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:54,760
But I really
wanted glasses.

420
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:56,960
Oh. Hmm.

421
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:59,919
I suppose you could have
some sunglasses.

422
00:17:59,919 --> 00:18:02,240
Yes! Sunglasses.

423
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,879
Here you are.

424
00:18:03,879 --> 00:18:07,200
[LAUGHS]
Fantastic.

425
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:10,879
I hope it's sunny
every day,

426
00:18:10,879 --> 00:18:14,200
so I can always
wear my sunglasses.

427
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:16,879
[ALL LAUGH]

428
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,200
[♪♪]

429
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,399
[GIGGLING, SNORTING]

430
00:18:21,399 --> 00:18:22,800
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

431
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:26,040
[SNORTING, LAUGHING]

432
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,760
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

433
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:30,120
[GRUNTING, CHUCKLING]

434
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:31,639
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

435
00:18:31,639 --> 00:18:33,360
[GRUNTING]

